Second: three temporary labels

Put these on the Selected Video screen, play the app, and tell me what each shows.

Label 1 — is the video URL arriving?

locSelectedVideoGUID

Label 2 — did the transcript load?

"Chars: " & Len(varVtt) & " | Cues: " & CountRows(colCues)

Label 3 — is the screen stuck in expanded mode?

"Big: " & varBig & " | W: " & Video1.Width & " | H: " & Video1.Height
What the answers will mean
Label 1	Meaning
Full https://…mp4 URL	The video has its source; the problem is the control or its layering
Blank	Navigate isn't passing it, so Video1.Media has nothing to play
Label 2	Meaning
Chars 20000+, Cues 199	Flow and parsing both fine; the caption control is the issue
Chars 0, Cues 0	OnVisible isn't reaching the flow, or the output name changed on re-add
Label 3	Meaning
Big: true	Stuck expanded, so controls may sit off-screen
W: 0 or H: 0	The video is collapsed to nothing — a sizing formula broke
